## 4. Why glasses_app might NOT auto-connect while PKG does

### A. Most likely: empty device history in `glasses_app` (cross-app)

If you connected only in PKG showcase, `glasses_app` has **no record** to reconnect to:

| App | Namespace | Storage key | Bundle / applicationId |
|---|---|---|---|
| PKG | `pkg_showcase` | `pkg_showcase_feature_device_connect.connected_devices` | `com.example.pkg_showcase` / `com.example.pkgShowcase` |
| glasses_app | `glasses_app` | `glasses_app_feature_device_connect.connected_devices` | `com.smartdevice.platform.glasses_app` / `com.smartdevice.platform.glassesApp` |

Auto-connect bails silently when `devices.isEmpty` (line 27–29 above).  
**“Previously paired in iOS/Android settings” is not consulted.**

On **iOS**, BLE `deviceId` (CBPeripheral UUID) is also **per-app**, so even copying SharedPreferences would not help across apps.

### B. No “already connected at OS level” detection

If the glasses are already GATT-connected (e.g. from native app or prior session), Flutter still starts with:

```6:26:/Users/jace/Documents/newapp/packages/core/core_ble/lib/src/model/ble_session_state.dart
  const BleSessionState({
    this.connectionState = BleConnectionState.disconnected,
    // ...
  });
  bool get isConnected => connectionState == BleConnectionState.connected;
```

`tryOnce()` does **not** skip because OS is connected — it only skips if `bleSessionProvider.isConnected` (app session). So “device looks connected in Settings but app shows offline” is expected until auto-connect succeeds.

### C. iOS permission preflight may fail in `glasses_app`

`BlePermissionGate` requires **both** Bluetooth and location:

```12:15:/Users/jace/Documents/newapp/packages/core/core_permission/lib/src/service/ble_permission_gate.dart
    for (final permission in [
      AppPermission.bluetooth,
      AppPermission.locationWhenInUse,
    ]) {
```

**PKG `Info.plist`** has location usage string:

```11:12:/Users/jace/Documents/newapp/apps/pkg_showcase/ios/Runner/Info.plist
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>扫描附近蓝牙设备需要位置权限。</string>
```

**glasses_app `Info.plist`** — `NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription` only; **no** `NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription`:

```56:59:/Users/jace/Documents/newapp/apps/glasses_app/ios/Runner/Info.plist
	<key>NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Bluetooth is used to discover and connect to your smart glasses.</string>
```

On iOS, missing that key can cause location permission request to fail → `_preflight()` returns false → auto-connect aborts with `permission.denied` recorded on the device record. PKG can pass this step.

### D. Connect succeeds then identity sync drops the link (both apps)

If auto-connect reaches GATT but `GlassesDeviceInfoEvent` never arrives within ~40s, `DeviceIdentitySyncController` calls `disconnect()`. That affects both apps equally after connect, but can make it **look** like auto-connect “didn’t stick.”

### E. What is NOT a difference

- Same `DeviceAutoConnectGate` placement and timing in both roots  
- Same `FlutterBlueBleService()` override  
- Same `deviceConnectControllerProvider.connect()` path  
- Same retry policy (6 attempts, 5s delay)  
- Android manifests both declare `BLUETOOTH_SCAN`, `BLUETOOTH_CONNECT`, `ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION`

---

## 5. Debugging checklist

1. **In glasses_app**, after a manual connect once, kill and relaunch — if auto-connect then works, root cause is **empty history / cross-app namespace**, not missing wiring.  
2. Inspect SharedPreferences key `glasses_app_feature_device_connect.connected_devices` on device.  
3. On iOS, watch logs for `permission.denied` from auto-connect preflight; compare with PKG on same device.  
4. Confirm you are not expecting **system-paired** or **OS-connected** restore — that path is unimplemented in this codebase.

